      "content": "that hybrid thing sounds okay in theory but it feels like a cop-out to avoid the actual issue. if we know that retributive systems are fundamentally broken and perpetuate systemic harm, isn't it more intellectually honest to just admit that restorative justice is the superior moral framework for a modern democracy? it feels like anything else is just defending an outdated system of harm.",
